      "line": 152,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "💡 **SUGGESTION: AC2 could also pin the retry's `path` (and `retention-days`)**\n\nAC2 asserts the retry rides the same digest pin, fires on the same id's failed outcome, sets `overwrite: true`, and re-uploads the same artifact `name` — but not that it uploads the same **path**. A drifted retry `path` (e.g. after a rename of `coverage/lcov.info` or the junit dir) would still satisfy every current assert while uploading wrong/empty content under the correct artifact name — silently poisoning what `coverage-gate` and `shard-rebalance.yml` download.\n\nOne-line addition inside the same loop:\n\n```dart\n        expect(\n          (retry['with'] as YamlMap)['path'],\n          (step['with'] as YamlMap)['path'],\n          reason:\n              'the retry of \"$id\" must re-upload the SAME path '\n              'the coverage merge / rebalancer reads',\n        );\n```\n\n(`retention-days` equality is a nice-to-have; `path` is the one that guards evidence integrity. The pty guard `ci_pty_artifact_upload_retry_guard_test.dart` has the same gap — worth fixing both while here, or leaving both as-is for symmetry.)"
    }
  ],
